r←onTimeout args;m;conns
⍝ Reap sessions whose socket died without a graceful Close signal.

⍝ The guard used to be `2=⎕NC'WSS.Conx'`, which is ALWAYS FALSE: Conx is a
⍝ `:field public` on the wss instance, and ⎕NC does not classify through an
⍝ instance reference — it returns 0 for both 'WSS.Conx' and (from inside)
⍝ 'Conx'. So this reaper never ran, and any connection lost without the
⍝ client's {"Signal":{"Name":"Close"}} leaked its session, thread and (in
⍝ Multi mode) its cloned namespace forever. ⎕NC'WSS' does classify (9), and
⍝ Conx is initialised with the instance, so it is safe to read once WSS exists.

⍝ Trapped because this runs on the Listen thread: an error escaping here
⍝ suspends that thread and wedges the entire server for every user.

:Trap 0
    :If 9=⎕NC 'WSS'
    :AndIf 0≠≢conns←WSS.Conx[;1]
    :AndIf ∨/m←~WSS.LDRC.Exists¨conns
        endSession¨{0 ⍵ 'Close'}¨m/conns
    :EndIf
:Else
    'E' Log 'onTimeout failed: ',⊃⎕DMX.DM
:EndTrap
